    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="0866" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Austria)/7–2045:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 776<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador
                        in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-20">July 20, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 143. Action AmEmbassy London,
                    information Department of State Washington, D. C. AFHQ Caserta, Italy please
                    pass USPolAd Florence, Italy.</p>
                <p>The President has approved the draft agreements on control machinery in Austria
                    and Zones of Occupation in Austria as recommended by the EAC. You are authorized
                    to sign<anchor n="1" xml:id="d776-f1"/> these agreements on behalf of the US
                    Government and to notify the EAC of their approval by the US Government.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d776-f1" n="1" xml:id="d776-f1-content">
                <p>The agreements had already been signed <hi rendition="#italic">ad
                    referendum</hi>. Their approval was discussed at the Fourth Plenary Meeting,
                    July 20. See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg176">p.
                        176</ref>. Notification of approval by the United States Government was
                    given on July 24.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
